  "paper_id": "ccs-2025-pulse-parallel-private-set-union-for-large-scale-entitie-186bd713",
  "title": "PULSE: Parallel Private Set Union for Large-Scale Entities",
  "abstract": "Multi-party private set union (mPSU) allows multiple parties to compute the union of their private input sets without revealing any additional information. Existing efficient mPSU protocols can be categorized into symmetric key encryption (SKE)-based and public key encryption (PKE)-based approaches. However, neither type of mPSU protocol scales efficiently to a large number of parties, as they fail to fully utilize available computational resources, leaving participants idle during various stages of the protocol execution.",
